4. https://www.codeproject.com/Articles/420447/5-practical-examples-of-PEX-framework-property-based-testi"

"1. To test the contract of an ArrayList class, we will need to create a list (using the Add method) and ensure that the operations to retrieve and remove elements do not change the order of the elements while the tests are executing. After an operation is done, we will call the methods on the list and compare the output with the expected results.

2. As the user can only add elements to the list, we do not need to check for the 'remove' operation. Here we will be testing the 'search' operation. In the 'remove' method, we need to check whether the removed item is in the list or not. If it is in the list, we can remove it again and check that it is not in the list after the second removal.

3. The sort operation can change the order of the list elements. Therefore, we need to preserve the order before the 'sort' operation and check that after--------------------        Debug.Assert(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX <= New_arrListCount);

        }
    }
