// Assertions in a separate methods due to the following reasons:
// 1. Pex Method contracts are generally expected to be pure, meaning no side effects. 
//     - I used a separate method for assertion as the assertions modify the state of objects under test.
// 2. The contracts also do not support return specifications as they are used to verify the method implementation
//     - Therefore a separate assertion method is kept for these cases.




